# NOTICE — sources of this project

This project is original work about the Fujifilm X-Pro3 2.00 firmware. It
stands on four upstream projects, cited below with what was taken from each.
Nothing in this repository contains Fujifilm firmware bytes.

## Fujifilm X-Pro3 2.00 update (`FWUP0021.DAT`)

- **Proprietary.** Not distributed here, not linked, not mirrored.
- SHA-256 `30ca22af2e1341c65d8f0637cc5e3ec675628cee8f517de0f1275bb5725c9f39`,
  50 087 104 bytes.
- Obtainable only from Fujifilm. Every tool and test in this repository takes
  the file as an argument, and the tests skip themselves when it is absent.
- The decompiled excerpts in `evidence/decompile/` are analysis output derived
  from that file, published for interoperability research. They are not a
  redistribution of it.

## `justjake/fujimod` — https://github.com/justjake/fujimod

- **GPL-2.0-only.** This project is distributed under the same licence.
- The bench (`bench/xpro3-bench/`) is written against its emulator and catalog
  crates and links them: `fujimod-emulator-boot`, `fujimod-catalog`,
  `fujimod-catalog-configuration`, `fujimod-catalog-resolution`,
  `fujimod-emulator-exr2-board`, `fujimod-emulator-models`.
- The run configuration in `configs/` follows its `RunConfiguration` schema.
- Upstream is the original project; this is not a fork of it. The bench is a
  workspace member that is installed into a fujimod checkout (see
  `scripts/install-bench.sh`) precisely so the two stay separable.
- Its emulator runtime links Unicorn Engine through `justjake/unicorn`
  (GPL-2.0).

## `cdeschenes/fujifilm-xFW` — https://github.com/cdeschenes/fujifilm-xFW

- **MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Cody Deschenes.** Full text in
  `LICENSES/fujifilm-xFW-MIT.txt`.
- `evidence/xpro3-2.00-baseline.json` is its `X-Pro3/analysis/baseline.json`
  for this exact update: two FFLZ segments with load addresses, the raw image,
  the content map, string fingerprints. The segment map in
  `bench/xpro3-bench/src/dispatch.rs` is derived from it.
- Its `CROSS-MODEL-COMPARISON.md` supplied the cross-model function addresses
